1. PURPOSE
----------
Single reference for how the business (IT) and control (OT) networks are
laid out, which zone each system belongs to, and which traffic is permitted
between zones. The model follows the Purdue Enterprise Reference Architecture
(ISA/IEC 62443 zones & conduits) as recommended in the CISA/EPA water sector
guidance. Changes to any conduit below require an approved CHG ticket signed
by both IT and Engineering.

2. ZONES
--------
 Purdue | Zone                     | VLAN | Subnet              | Gateway
 -------+--------------------------+------+---------------------+---------------
 L5/DMZ | Internet DMZ             |  10  | {{ '%-19s' | format(ww_net ~ '.10.0/24') }} | {{ ww_net }}.10.254
 L4     | Corporate IT             |  20  | {{ '%-19s' | format(ww_net ~ '.20.0/24') }} | {{ ww_net }}.20.254
 L3.5   | OT DMZ                   |  30  | {{ '%-19s' | format(ww_net ~ '.30.0/24') }} | {{ ww_net }}.30.254
 L2/L3  | SCADA Control Center     |  40  | {{ '%-19s' | format(ww_net ~ '.40.0/24') }} | {{ ww_net }}.40.254
 L1     | Field Controllers        |  50  | {{ '%-19s' | format(ww_net ~ '.50.0/24') }} | {{ ww_net }}.50.254
 L0     | Field I/O (hardwired 4-20 mA / discrete - no IP)

All inter-zone routing is done by the core firewall. Default policy between
zones is DENY; only the conduits listed in section 4 are permitted.

