4. CONDUITS (PERMITTED INTER-ZONE TRAFFIC)
------------------------------------------
 #  | Source            | Destination        | Port(s)      | Purpose / ticket
 ---+-------------------+--------------------+--------------+-------------------------------
 1  | Internet          | ww-web01           | 80, 443      | Public website / portal
 2  | ww-web01          | ww-fs01            | tcp/445      | CCR report sync (svc acct)
 3  | ww-web01          | Corporate VLAN 20  | tcp/22       | TEMPORARY - CHG-2023-114 web
    |                   |                    |              | server migration. Was due to be
    |                   |                    |              | removed after cutover (Q4 2023).
    |                   |                    |              | ** still open - see note A **
 4  | Corporate VLAN 20 | ww-web01           | tcp/22, 80   | Website content management
 5  | Corporate VLAN 20 | ww-hist01          | tcp/8080     | Trend viewing from the office
 6  | ww-it01           | ww-jump01          | tcp/22       | IT admin access to OT (key only)
 7  | ww-hist01         | ww-hmi01           | tcp/80       | Historian tag collection (API)
 8  | ww-jump01         | ww-hmi01           | tcp/80, 5900 | Remote HMI support (web + VNC)
 9  | ww-jump01         | ww-eng01           | tcp/22       | Remote engineering / vendor
 10 | ww-hmi01          | Field VLAN 50      | tcp/502      | SCADA polling (Modbus/TCP)
 11 | ww-eng01          | Field VLAN 50      | tcp/502,     | Programming / diagnostics
    |                   |                    | tcp/20256    | (Modbus/TCP, Unitronics PCOM)

 Note A: The CHG-2023-114 rule lets the DMZ web server open SSH sessions to
 ANY host on the corporate VLAN "temporarily" while the old website was
 migrated. Cutover finished Nov 2023. Removal is tracked in the FY27 firewall
 cleanup item (see Board minutes 2026-04-16, item 4b - deferred).

 Note B: Nothing in the SCADA (40) or Field (50) zones may initiate a
 connection to Corporate or the Internet. Vendor support enters only through
 ww-jump01 (see SCADA\OT_Remote_Access_SOP.txt).

